## About this package

This package is part of the ${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MAJOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MINOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_PATCH} release of Emgu LiteRT. It contains:

- `Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Chat.dll`: the conversation logic of a chat, without UI, over any `IChatClient` ([Microsoft.Extensions.AI](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/ai/microsoft-extensions-ai)). `ChatConversation` keeps the messages and their attachments, streams replies with their thinking and tool steps, and keeps the conversation within the model's context window by summarizing or dropping earlier messages. Token counting comes from the on-device `${EMGU_LITERT_LM_MODELS_NUGET_ID}` language models (through `${EMGU_LITERT_LM_EXTENSIONS_AI_NUGET_ID}`) when one is used.

`${EMGU_LITERT_LM_MAUI_CONTROL_NUGET_ID}`'s chat control is built on this package. Apps with their own UI, or no MAUI, can use it directly: its types raise `PropertyChanged` / `CollectionChanged`, so any UI can bind to them.

## Getting Started

The language models run on the device through LiteRT-LM: add the LiteRT-LM native runtime package for your platform, as for `${EMGU_LITERT_LM_MODELS_NUGET_ID}`.

```csharp
using Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Chat;
using Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Models;

using (Qwen3 model = new Qwen3())
{
    await model.Init();   // downloads the model on first use
    ChatConversation chat = new ChatConversation(model) { Instructions = "Keep your answers short." };
    ChatMessageItem reply = await chat.SendAsync("What is the capital of France?");
    Console.WriteLine(reply.Text);
    reply = await chat.SendAsync("And of Italy?");   // the conversation goes on
    Console.WriteLine(reply.Text);
}
```

`chat.Messages` is an `ObservableCollection<ChatMessageItem>`: the user's messages and the replies. While a reply streams, its `Text`, `Thinking` and `Steps` change as they arrive (`IsStreaming`, `IsThinking`); afterwards its `State` is `Done`, `Interrupted` (cancelled: it keeps what was written) or `Failed` (`Error` says why).

### Tools, thinking and other providers

Give the conversation a client that calls tools, and the model's tool calls show as the reply's `Steps` (`ChatClientBuilder` and `UseFunctionInvocation` come from the `Microsoft.Extensions.AI` package; the tools from `${EMGU_LITERT_LM_AGENTS_NUGET_ID}`):

```csharp
using Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Agents;
using Emgu.LiteRT.LM.Extensions.AI;
using Microsoft.Extensions.AI;

Gemma4E2B model = new Gemma4E2B();
await model.Init();
IChatClient client = new ChatClientBuilder(model.AsIChatClient()).UseFunctionInvocation().Build();
ChatConversation chat = new ChatConversation(client, model);   // the model counts tokens and sets the context window
ChatOptions options = new ChatOptions
{
    Tools = new List<AITool> { AgentTools.Calculate(), AgentTools.Weather() },
    Reasoning = new ReasoningOptions { Effort = ReasoningEffort.Medium }   // thinking; ReasoningEffort.None turns it off
};
ChatMessageItem reply = await chat.SendAsync("What's the weather in Paris?", options: options);
```

Any other `IChatClient` works too (a server, another provider); without a `LanguageModel`, tokens are estimated (set `CountTokens` and `ContextWindow` to do better). `SendAsync` also takes images and audio (`DataContent`, for models that take them), a `context` - text the model is given before the message but that isn't shown, e.g. document excerpts - and a `client` for that message only (e.g. one that runs a multi-step task). `RegenerateAsync(reply)` sends the latest message again into the same reply.

### Long conversations

Before each message the conversation counts its tokens. If the message wouldn't fit in `ContextWindow` (less `ReplyReserveTokens` for the reply), the earlier messages are summarized by the model (`Compaction = ChatCompaction.Summarize`, the default) or dropped (`ChatCompaction.Drop`, better for small models). The transcript keeps every message: `ContextStart` is the first one the model still sees and `Summary` the summary of those before it (`Compacted` is raised). `CompactAsync()` compacts now and `GetContextUsageAsync()` tells how full the window is. If the model still reports the context full, the earlier messages are dropped and the message is sent once more.

### Saving and reopening

`ExchangeCompleted` is raised after each reply: save the message and the reply then. To reopen a chat, build its `ChatMessageItem`s and call `Load(messages, summary, contextStart)`; the next message gives the model the conversation again.

### For apps

- `ChatMessageItem.Decorations`: your own objects (or views) shown with a message, e.g. cards above a reply; `ChatMessageItem.Tag`: your own data for a message; `ChatMessageItem.Transcript`: a voice message's words, shown but never given to the model (it hears the audio).
- `AddNotice(content, text)`: a transcript item the model never sees, e.g. an alert.
- `ChatToolStep`: step lines of your own ("Looked in report.pdf...").
- `BeforeStreaming`: runs after any compaction and before the reply streams, e.g. to change the message's `Context`.
- `ModelLoadState`: downloading and loading a `LanguageModel` for a UI - stage, progress, errors, `LoadAsync` / `Cancel`.
- `ReplyMarkdown` (the Markdown of replies, read without UI) and `ReplySpeechText` (a reply as text to read aloud).
- `VoiceLanguages`: languages for a speech recognizer, e.g. for a language setting (`Resolve`, `NameOf`).

